----------------------------------------------------------------------
## 0. Purpose
This spec defines the REQUIRED header fields and integrity anchors for all governance artifacts.
Artifacts MUST be machine-parseable and compatible with canonical JSON hashing rules.

----------------------------------------------------------------------

## 1. Artifact Header — Common Fields (REQUIRED)

Every governance artifact MUST contain:

1) artifact_type (string)
   - Meaning: High-level category for routing / policy checks.
   - Examples: "GOV_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE", "TRACE_BUNDLE", "RESET_DECLARATION", "APPROVAL_BUNDLE"

2) artifact_version (string)
   - Meaning: Contract version identifier.
   - Examples: "EVIDENCE_v1", "TRACE_v1", "RESET_DECLARATION_v1"

3) created_at_utc (string, RFC3339/ISO8601, trailing "Z")
   - Format: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS(.ffffff)?Z
   - NOTE: Use "Z" timezone. Microseconds are allowed.
   - Example: "2026-02-12T10:19:31.064273Z"

4) meta (object)
   REQUIRED keys:
   - meta.created_at_utc (string): must equal top-level created_at_utc
   - meta.node_id (string): runtime node identifier (may be "UNKNOWN_NODE" in dev)
   - meta.git_commit (string): build commit (may be "UNKNOWN_COMMIT" in dev)

5) integrity (object)  **(REQUIRED even if values are null in dev)**
   REQUIRED keys:
   - integrity.payload_sha256 (string|null)
     - SHA256 of canonical JSON payload excluding "integrity" itself.
   - integrity.prev_chain_hash (string|null)
     - MUST mirror chain.prev_hash when chain exists.
   - integrity.signatures (array)
     - Each item:
       - tier (string): "T1" | "T2" | "T3"
       - signer_id (string)
       - signature (string)
       - signed_at_utc (string)

6) evidence_binding (object)  **(REQUIRED for Evidence-like artifacts)**
   REQUIRED keys:
   - evidence_required (boolean)
   - evidence_type (string)
   - evidence_version (string)
   - schema_set_ref (string|null)
   - validator_version (string|null)

7) chain (object|null)
   - For chain-aware artifacts, chain MUST exist.
   REQUIRED keys when chain exists:
   - chain.prev_hash (string|null)
   - chain.this_hash (string)

----------------------------------------------------------------------

## 2. Evidence-Type Enum (LOCKED LIST v1.0)

The following evidence_type values are RESERVED in v1.0:

- GOV_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE
- TRACE_BUNDLE
- RESET_DECLARATION
- APPROVAL_BUNDLE

Rule:
- New values require Amendment Procedure.

----------------------------------------------------------------------

## 3. Evidence Chain Binding (R1–R4 Binding)

If an artifact declares chain, then:

- chain.this_hash MUST be present.
- chain.prev_hash MUST be present unless it is a system-first GENESIS.

GENESIS rule:
- chain.prev_hash MAY be "GENESIS" OR null ONLY for the first genesis declaration in a chain.
- Any additional GENESIS requires Reset Policy (separate governance).

Binding rule:
- integrity.prev_chain_hash MUST equal chain.prev_hash (string-equal), or both null for system-first GENESIS.

----------------------------------------------------------------------

## 4. Evidence Writer Minimal Compliance Profile (derived from current runtime evidence)

This section is normative for "GOV_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE" artifacts produced by governance_writer.

A GOV_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE artifact MUST include these top-level keys:

- evidence_type
- evidence_version
- created_at_utc
- meta
- inputs
- summary
- result
- chain

And MUST satisfy:
- meta.created_at_utc == created_at_utc
- inputs.bundle_path (string)
- inputs.bundle_sha256 (string, 64 hex)
- chain.prev_hash (string|"GENESIS"|null)
- chain.this_hash (string, 64 hex)
- result.schema_set_ref (string)
- result.validator_version (string)

----------------------------------------------------------------------

## 5. Failure Semantics (Fail-Closed)

If any REQUIRED field is missing or invalid:
- status MUST be FAIL_CLOSED at the consuming policy layer (HARD or SOFT).
- the artifact MAY still be persisted for forensics.
- downstream execution MUST NOT proceed without explicit override procedure.

----------------------------------------------------------------------

## 6. Compatibility Notes (Non-breaking evolution)

Allowed non-breaking additions:
- Add new OPTIONAL fields inside meta/result/summary/inputs.
- Add new evidence_binding subfields marked OPTIONAL.

Forbidden without amendment:
- Renaming required keys
- Changing meanings of existing enums
- Changing chain hashing rules

----------------------------------------------------------------------

